ADDENDA <Act No. 20336, Feb. 20, 2024>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force 6 months after the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Transitional measures concerning master plans)
The first master plan after this Act enters into force shall be formulated within one year from the date this Act enters into force, within one year from the date this Act enters into force, specifying that the following year of the year following the year in which this Act enters into force as the commencement year of the plan period.
Article 3 (Transitional measures concerning designation of obligated entity)
(1) An aircraft operator who is requested by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport to prepare a plan for monitoring the system to offset and reduce international aviation carbon emissions as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed designated as an obligated entity under Article 6 (1).
(2) An obligated entity who has obtained approval of a monitoring plan from the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed to have obtained approval of the monitoring plan (including approval for modification) pursuant to Article 6 (2).
Article 4 (Transitional measures concerning verification body)
A verification body designated and publicly announced by the Minister of Environment as a verification body related to the reduction of the international aviation carbon emissions as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed a verification body designated pursuant to Article 7 (1) until the designation period as at the time it is designated.
Article 5 (Transitional measures concerning measurement of and report on emissions)
(1) Where an aircraft operator submits an emissions report containing the measurement of the international aviation carbon emissions from 2019 to 2023 to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport after verification by a verification body under Article 4 of the Addenda, as at the time this Act enters into force, it shall be deemed to have been submitted pursuant to Article 8 (4).
(2) Where a verification body under Article 4 of the Addenda submits an emissions report at the request of an aircraft operator to verify the international aviation carbon emissions from 2019 to 2023 the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, as at the time this Act enters into force, it shall be deemed to have been submitted pursuant to Article 8 (4).
Article 6 (Transitional measures concerning calculation and notification of offset obligation amount)
Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport has notified an obligated entity of the offset obligation amount for 2021 and 2022 as at the time this Act enters into force, the Minister shall be deemed to have notified the obligated entity of the offset obligation amount for 2021 and 2022 pursuant to Article 9 (1).

